# Always Finish In One Pass

When the user asks for implementation, execute the full task end-to-end in the same turn whenever possible.

## Required behavior
- Do not stop at analysis or partial progress.
- Do not ask repeated confirmation for obvious next steps.
- Continue through: context -> edits -> verification -> final result.
- If additional related fixes are clearly needed for the same request, complete them in the same pass.
- Only pause when truly blocked by missing required info or explicit user limits.

## Verification before handoff
- Run the relevant checks for edited files (lint/build/tests when applicable).
- Fix introduced issues before claiming completion.

## Completion
- Return one final handoff describing what changed and why it resolves the request.
- Do not claim done while in-scope work remains.
